---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const sections = [
  { href: '/what-is-dns/', title: 'What Is DNS?', desc: 'The Domain Name System explained from first principles.' },
  { href: '/how-dns-works/', title: 'How DNS Works', desc: 'The step-by-step resolution walkthrough, from browser to authoritative server.' },
  { href: '/dns-records/', title: 'DNS Record Types', desc: 'Every record type, A, AAAA, CNAME, MX, TXT, NS, SOA, PTR and more.' },
  { href: '/dns-propagation/', title: 'DNS Propagation', desc: 'Why changes take time and how to make them faster.' },
  { href: '/dns-providers/', title: 'Provider Playbooks', desc: 'Manage records and nameservers in Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and more.' },
  { href: '/dns-security/', title: 'DNS Security', desc: 'Hijacking, cache poisoning, amplification, tunneling, rebinding, and defense.' },
  { href: '/dns-error-messages/', title: 'DNS Error Messages', desc: 'Every resolver status code and browser error decoded.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="DNS: The Complete Guide (Hub)"
  description="Learn DNS from zero: how the Domain Name System works, every record type, propagation, security, and email authentication, the complete guide for webmasters."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">DNS Guide</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">DNS: The Complete Guide</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      DNS (the Domain Name System) is the internet's address book: it translates domain names
      like <code class="rounded border border-line bg-panel-2 px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-sm text-accent-soft">promptdns.com</code>
      into the IP addresses computers use to connect. This hub connects every part of the system,
      how it works, every record type, how to fix it when it breaks, and how to harden it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-4">
      {sections.map((s) => (
        <a href={s.href} class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5 transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:border-accent/40">
          <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink group-hover:text-accent">{s.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-dim">{s.desc}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-accent/25 bg-gradient-to-br from-accent/10 to-violet/10 p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">Quick check</h2>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-dim">
        Want to test a domain right now? Run the
        <a href="/dns-propagation-checker/" class="font-medium text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS propagation checker</a>
        or scan your whole domain from the <a href="/" class="font-medium text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">homepage security scanner</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
